      "side": 1,
      "message": "How about we just generate and copy the assembly instructions into an array for the trivial function you are trying to call:\n\n```\nstatic int func1(void)\n{\n\treturn EC_SUCCESS;\n}\n```\n\ne.g., generate the assembly and then copy the instructions into an array (with an annotation of what each instruction is):\n\n```\nrm -rf build \u0026\u0026 make BOARD\u003dhelipilot test-ram_lock -j\nllvm-objdump -S -d ./build/helipilot/ram_lock/RW/ram_lock.RW.elf\n```\n\nIt looks like we can implement it with two instructions:\n\n```\n10085818 \u003cfunc1\u003e:\n;       return EC_SUCCESS;\n10085818: 2000          movs    r0, #0x0\n1008581a: 4770          bx      lr\n```\n\nI think that will be a lot easier to read than trying to hijack an existing unrelated section (`.lowpower_ram`).",
